He gave DJ the dynamite.

00:33:13.881 --> 00:33:16.362
"'Take this,' he said.

00:33:16.423 --> 00:33:17.903
I started it.

00:33:17.963 --> 00:33:19.354
You finish it.

00:33:19.414 --> 00:33:21.265
The dynamite's ready.

00:33:21.325 --> 00:33:25.457
You have three minutes and 18 seconds."

00:33:25.517 --> 00:33:27.488
DJ looked at the house.

00:33:27.508 --> 00:33:30.460
"'Where do I throw it?'

00:33:30.520 --> 00:33:31.918
he thought.

00:33:31.978 --> 00:33:38.899
Then he saw the smoke and remembered the fire, the heart.

00:33:38.959 --> 00:33:43.030
The digger and the house were now face to face.

00:33:43.090 --> 00:33:48.642
Then DJ saw the tall crane high over the danger zone.

00:33:48.702 --> 00:33:51.233
Chowder, he shouted.

00:33:51.293 --> 00:33:55.696
Try to move the house under the crane.

00:33:55.756 --> 00:34:00.480
Suddenly the digger turned and moved to the crane.

00:34:00.540 --> 00:34:04.152
The house tried to turn, but it fell.

00:34:04.212 --> 00:34:06.574
There was a loud sound.

00:34:06.634 --> 00:34:09.575
The house started to break.

00:34:09.635 --> 00:34:14.617
There were parts of the house all over the danger zone.

00:34:14.678 --> 00:34:18.349
DJ and Jenny went up in the crane.

00:34:18.410 --> 00:34:20.711
But where was Chowder?

00:34:20.770 --> 00:34:22.978
Then they heard him.

00:34:23.038 --> 00:34:25.694
Hey, shouted Chowder.

00:34:25.754 --> 00:34:27.845
I did it!

00:34:27.865 --> 00:34:28.175
Me!

00:34:28.235 --> 00:34:30.626
The house is dead!

00:34:30.686 --> 00:34:32.688
But it wasn't dead.

00:34:32.748 --> 00:34:38.690
All the parts of the house came back together again to make a new house.

00:34:38.750 --> 00:34:42.832
This time it was a worse monster than before.

00:34:42.892 --> 00:34:45.496
It looked terrible.

00:34:45.556 --> 00:34:49.690
Chowder drove the digger quickly to the crane.

00:34:49.750 --> 00:34:52.632
The new monster house followed.

00:34:52.692 --> 00:34:57.534
The door opened and the mouth closed on the arm of the digger.

00:34:57.594 --> 00:35:00.025
It took the digger up high.

00:35:00.086 --> 00:35:04.237
Chowder fell out and then the tongue took the digger.

00:35:04.298 --> 00:35:05.938
Chowder ran.

00:35:05.998 --> 00:35:08.300
The house followed.

00:35:08.360 --> 00:35:11.681
DJ looked down the arm of the crane.

00:35:11.741 --> 00:35:13.178
He was frightened.

00:35:13.238 --> 00:35:15.664
I can't do it," he said.

00:35:15.724 --> 00:35:19.795
You can, said Jenny, and she smiled at him.

00:35:19.855 --> 00:35:23.776
Yes, he thought, or can.

00:35:23.836 --> 00:35:26.978
He moved to the end of the arm.

00:35:27.038 --> 00:35:29.308
DJ looked down.

00:35:29.368 --> 00:35:31.309
There was the house.

00:35:31.369 --> 00:35:33.680
There was the smoke.

00:35:33.740 --> 00:35:40.192
DJ threw the dynamite into the smoke, into the heart of the house.

00:35:40.252 --> 00:35:43.413
Everything was very quiet.

00:35:43.473 --> 00:35:45.844
The house didn't move.

00:35:45.904 --> 00:35:48.974
It didn't look like a monster house now.

00:35:49.034 --> 00:35:52.656
It looked clean and quiet like before.

00:35:52.716 --> 00:35:55.106
The kids waited.

00:35:55.166 --> 00:35:57.037
Was it over?

00:35:57.097 --> 00:36:01.288
Did DJ throw the dynamite in the right place?

00:36:01.348 --> 00:36:05.869
Little sounds started to come from the house.

00:36:05.929 --> 00:36:08.948
Then they were bigger and louder.

00:36:09.008 --> 00:36:16.058
Suddenly, there was a great white light, and the house was a ball of fire.

00:36:16.118 --> 00:36:22.831
Cement, windows, walls and floor rained down from the sky.

00:36:22.891 --> 00:36:25.892
The kids shouted and danced.

00:36:25.952 --> 00:36:27.513
We did it!

00:36:27.573 --> 00:36:29.904
The house is dead!

00:36:29.964 --> 00:36:32.812
Then something happened.

00:36:32.872 --> 00:36:37.544
A strong wind came and moved all the parts of the house.

00:36:37.604 --> 00:36:40.666
They all came together in the sky.

00:36:40.726 --> 00:36:42.698
It was Constance.

00:36:42.758 --> 00:36:45.531
Big and beautiful again.

00:36:45.591 --> 00:36:50.096
Constance, said DJ quietly.

00:36:50.156 --> 00:36:53.018
Mr. Nebbercracker looked up.

00:36:53.078 --> 00:36:54.830
My love!

00:36:54.890 --> 00:36:56.202
Goodbye!

00:36:56.222 --> 00:36:57.898
He cried.

00:36:57.958 --> 00:37:00.695
Constance smiled.

00:37:00.755 --> 00:37:04.457
She put her arms around Mr. Nebbercracker.

00:37:04.517 --> 00:37:09.810
Then the wind came again, and there was only the sky.

00:37:09.870 --> 00:37:17.534
I'm sorry about your house, um, wife, said DJ.

00:37:17.594 --> 00:37:22.547
Constance is happy now, said Mr. Nebbercracker.

00:37:22.607 --> 00:37:28.522
There was a light in his eyes, and I couldn't live my life.

00:37:28.582 --> 00:37:30.936
Thank you.

00:37:30.996 --> 00:37:33.938
It was Halloween night.

00:37:33.998 --> 00:37:37.890
There were trick-or-treaters on Mr. Nevercracker's lawn.

00:37:37.950 --> 00:37:40.541
They came to get their things.

00:37:40.601 --> 00:37:46.314
There were bikes, basketballs, footballs and kites.

00:37:46.374 --> 00:37:50.116
DJ gave the bike back to the little girl.

00:37:50.176 --> 00:37:54.058
Thank you, she said and smiled.

00:37:54.118 --> 00:37:59.404
Then she went between the trees and the lovely gardens of Oak Street.

00:37:59.464 --> 00:38:02.880
Jenny put her arms around the boys.

00:38:02.940 --> 00:38:07.683
We must do something together again soon, she said.

00:38:07.743 --> 00:38:10.554
Then she left with her mom.

00:38:10.614 --> 00:38:15.168
We are too old for treacle treating, said Chowder.

00:38:15.228 --> 00:38:17.530
Yes, said DJ.

00:38:17.590 --> 00:38:20.902
But we heard a very difficult evening.

00:38:20.962 --> 00:38:23.694
Yes, said DJ.

00:38:23.754 --> 00:38:26.005
Time for treats?

00:38:26.066 --> 00:38:29.051
Yeah, time for treats.

00:38:29.111 --> 00:38:32.598
and the boys ran down the road.

00:38:32.658 --> 00:38:38.324
Some people came out of the big hole in Mr. Nebbercracker's garden.

00:38:38.384 --> 00:38:40.696
Bones was first.

00:38:40.756 --> 00:38:43.399
He looked very surprised.

00:38:43.459 --> 00:38:46.872
Then the two policemen came out.

00:38:46.932 --> 00:38:49.073
Bones looked at them.

00:38:49.133 --> 00:38:53.155
Happy Halloween, he said, and smiled.

00:38:53.215 --> 00:38:56.336
He held his red kite in his hands.

00:38:56.397 --> 00:38:59.128
You too, said Landers.

00:38:59.188 --> 00:39:00.769
Happy Halloween.

